§ `Part V - Termination of residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 4 - Orders for termination of residential tenancy agreement`

§§§ `71. Application by lessor for termination and order for possession`

DECLARE `section 71 application` HAS
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination to the other under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the day specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the day specified` IS A NUMBER
    `the notice of termination was given immediately the rent breach occurred and the rent due is paid in full before the day specified` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice complied with and was given in accordance with this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon a particular ground prescribed by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given by a lessor on a ground referred to in section 71C or 71H` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has established that ground` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was upon the ground of a breach by the tenant of a term of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the breach is in all the circumstances such as to justify termination of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `giving the notice is retaliatory action taken by the lessor against the tenant because of a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has remedied the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon the ground referred to in section 69` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the consequences of the lessor continuing to be bound by the agreement would not be unduly burdensome to the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the period of 6 months before notice was given by the lessor the tenant complained to a public authority or took steps to secure or enforce the tenant's rights as a tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has proved that the lessor was not wholly or partly motivated to give notice by that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant is not eligible to reside in social housing premises or in the class of social housing premises to which the agreement relates under the criteria approved under section 71E` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has offered to enter into a new social housing tenancy agreement with the tenant in respect of alternative premises that are available for occupation by the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any notice required to be given under section 71F or 71I before giving notice of termination was given in accordance with that section` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any review required to be carried out under section 71F or 71I was carried out in accordance with that section` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71(1)
@export Decide whether the lessor may apply under s.71 for termination and possession
GIVEN a IS A `section 71 application` @desc Notice of termination under this Act except s.70A; tenant failed to deliver up possession on the specified day; application within 30 days after that day; not blocked by s.62(5)(a) (immediate rent notice with rent paid in full before the specified day).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lessor may apply under section 71` IF
        a's `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination to the other under this Act`
    AND NOT a's `the notice was given under section 70A`
    AND a's `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the day specified`
    AND a's `days after the day specified` AT MOST 30
    AND a's `days after the day specified` AT LEAST 0
    AND NOT a's `the notice of termination was given immediately the rent breach occurred and the rent due is paid in full before the day specified`

GIVEN a IS A `section 71 application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court is satisfied of the matters in section 71(2)` IF
        a's `the notice complied with and was given in accordance with this Act`
    AND (
            NOT a's `the notice was given by the lessor upon a particular ground prescribed by this Act`
        OR  (
                a's `the notice was given by a lessor on a ground referred to in section 71C or 71H`
            AND a's `any notice required to be given under section 71F or 71I before giving notice of termination was given in accordance with that section`
            AND a's `any review required to be carried out under section 71F or 71I was carried out in accordance with that section`
            AND (
                    a's `the tenant is not eligible to reside in social housing premises or in the class of social housing premises to which the agreement relates under the criteria approved under section 71E`
                OR  a's `the lessor has offered to enter into a new social housing tenancy agreement with the tenant in respect of alternative premises that are available for occupation by the tenant`
                )
            )
        OR  (
                a's `the lessor has established that ground`
            AND (
                    NOT a's `the notice was upon the ground of a breach by the tenant of a term of the agreement`
                OR  a's `the breach is in all the circumstances such as to justify termination of the agreement`
                )
            )
        )

GIVEN a IS A `section 71 application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may refuse to make the orders under section 71(3)(b)` IF
        a's `giving the notice is retaliatory action taken by the lessor against the tenant because of a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)`
    OR  (
            a's `the notice was upon the ground of a breach by the tenant of a term of the agreement`
        AND a's `the tenant has remedied the breach`
        )
    OR  (
            a's `the notice was given by the lessor upon the ground referred to in section 69`
        AND a's `the consequences of the lessor continuing to be bound by the agreement would not be unduly burdensome to the lessor`
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.71(2)
@export Decide whether the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under s.71(2)
GIVEN a IS A `section 71 application` @desc Subject to s.71(3), the court shall make the orders if satisfied the notice complied with this Act and, where given on a prescribed ground other than s.71C or 71H, that the lessor has established the ground (and for breach, that the breach justifies termination). The court may refuse if the notice is retaliatory, the tenant has remedied a breach, or a s.69 notice would not be unduly burdensome.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 71` IF
        `the lessor may apply under section 71` a
    AND `the court is satisfied of the matters in section 71(2)` a
    AND NOT `the court may refuse to make the orders under section 71(3)(b)` a

GIVEN a IS A `section 71 application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the burden lies on the lessor to prove that the lessor was not wholly or partly motivated to give notice by the tenant's complaint or enforcement steps` IF
        a's `within the period of 6 months before notice was given by the lessor the tenant complained to a public authority or took steps to secure or enforce the tenant's rights as a tenant`
    AND NOT a's `the lessor has proved that the lessor was not wholly or partly motivated to give notice by that fact`

§§§ `72. Application for termination and order for possession in relation to fixed term agreements`

DECLARE `section 72 application` HAS
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the possession day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the possession day` IS A NUMBER
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the term of the tenancy under the agreement is less than 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor genuinely proposed at the time the lessor entered into the agreement to use the premises after the expiration of the term for purposes inconsistent with the tenant continuing to occupy the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant of the tenant's own initiative sought a tenancy of a term of less than 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.72
@export Decide whether the court shall make orders terminating a fixed-term agreement and for possession under s.72
GIVEN a IS A `section 72 application` @desc s.70A notice given; tenant failed to deliver up on the possession day; application within 30 days. The court shall make the orders, but must refuse where the term is less than 90 days unless the lessor genuinely proposed an inconsistent use at entry or the tenant of the tenant's own initiative sought a term of less than 90 days. That 90-day refusal does not apply where the premises are the lessor's principal place of residence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 72` IF
        a's `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination under section 70A`
    AND a's `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the possession day`
    AND a's `days after the possession day` AT MOST 30
    AND a's `days after the possession day` AT LEAST 0
    AND (
            a's `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor`
        OR  NOT a's `the term of the tenancy under the agreement is less than 90 days`
        OR  a's `the lessor genuinely proposed at the time the lessor entered into the agreement to use the premises after the expiration of the term for purposes inconsistent with the tenant continuing to occupy the premises`
        OR  a's `the tenant of the tenant's own initiative sought a tenancy of a term of less than 90 days`
        )

§§§ `73A. Notice of termination not required in certain cases`

`an application under section 73, 74, 75A or 75 may be made whether or not notice of termination has been given` MEANS TRUE

§§§ `73. Termination of agreement where tenant causing serious damage or injury`

DECLARE `section 73 application` HAS
    `the applicant is the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, serious damage to the premises or, where relevant, a common area or chattels in the common area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, injury to the lessor, the property manager of the premises, or any person in occupation of or permitted on adjacent premises` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.73
@export Decide whether the court may terminate the agreement under s.73 for serious damage or injury
GIVEN a IS A `section 73 application` @desc Application by the lessor. The court may terminate if satisfied the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely to cause or permit, serious damage to the premises (or a common area or chattels in it) or injury to the lessor, the property manager, or a person in occupation of or permitted on adjacent premises. Notice of termination is not required (s.73A). If the court terminates, it shall also make an order for possession of immediate effect.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may terminate the agreement under section 73` IF
        a's `the applicant is the lessor`
    AND (
            a's `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, serious damage to the premises or, where relevant, a common area or chattels in the common area`
        OR  a's `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, injury to the lessor, the property manager of the premises, or any person in occupation of or permitted on adjacent premises`
        )

§§§ `74. Termination of agreement where lessor or tenant would otherwise suffer undue hardship`

DECLARE `section 74 application` HAS
    `the applicant is the lessor or the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor or tenant would in the circumstances of the case suffer undue hardship if required to terminate the agreement under any other provision of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.74
@export Decide whether the court may terminate the agreement under s.74 for undue hardship
GIVEN a IS A `section 74 application` @desc Application by the lessor or the tenant. The court may terminate if satisfied that person would suffer undue hardship if required to terminate under any other provision of this Act. Notice of termination is not required (s.73A).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may terminate the agreement under section 74` IF
        a's `the applicant is the lessor or the tenant`
    AND a's `the lessor or tenant would in the circumstances of the case suffer undue hardship if required to terminate the agreement under any other provision of this Act`

§§§ `75A. Termination of social housing tenancy agreement due to objectionable behaviour`

DECLARE `section 75A application` HAS
    `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is the lessor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has used the social housing premises, or caused or permitted the social housing premises to be used, for an illegal purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has caused or permitted a nuisance by the use of the social housing premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant has interfered, or caused or permitted any interference, with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of any person who resides in the immediate vicinity of the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the behaviour justifies terminating the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.75A
@export Decide whether the court may terminate a social housing tenancy agreement under s.75A for objectionable behaviour
GIVEN a IS A `section 75A application` @desc Application by the lessor under a social housing tenancy agreement. The court may terminate if satisfied of illegal use, nuisance, or interference with a neighbour's reasonable peace, comfort or privacy, and that the behaviour justifies terminating the agreement. Notice of termination is not required (s.73A).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may terminate the agreement under section 75A` IF
        a's `the agreement is a social housing tenancy agreement`
    AND a's `the applicant is the lessor`
    AND a's `the behaviour justifies terminating the agreement`
    AND (
            a's `the tenant has used the social housing premises, or caused or permitted the social housing premises to be used, for an illegal purpose`
        OR  a's `the tenant has caused or permitted a nuisance by the use of the social housing premises`
        OR  a's `the tenant has interfered, or caused or permitted any interference, with the reasonable peace, comfort or privacy of any person who resides in the immediate vicinity of the premises`
        )

§§§ `75. Termination of agreement for breach by lessor`

DECLARE `section 75 application` HAS
    `the applicant is the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor has breached the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the breach is in the circumstances of the case such as to justify termination of the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.75
@export Decide whether the court may terminate the agreement under s.75 for breach by the lessor
GIVEN a IS A `section 75 application` @desc Application by the tenant. The court may terminate if satisfied the lessor has breached the agreement and the breach is in the circumstances such as to justify termination. Notice of termination is not required (s.73A).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may terminate the agreement under section 75` IF
        a's `the applicant is the tenant`
    AND a's `the lessor has breached the agreement`
    AND a's `the breach is in the circumstances of the case such as to justify termination of the agreement`

§§ `Fixtures`

`s.71 breach notice tenant still in possession` MEANS `section 71 application` WITH
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination to the other under this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given under section 70A` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the day specified` IS TRUE,
    `days after the day specified` IS 10,
    `the notice of termination was given immediately the rent breach occurred and the rent due is paid in full before the day specified` IS FALSE,
    `the notice complied with and was given in accordance with this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon a particular ground prescribed by this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given by a lessor on a ground referred to in section 71C or 71H` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has established that ground` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was upon the ground of a breach by the tenant of a term of the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the breach is in all the circumstances such as to justify termination of the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `giving the notice is retaliatory action taken by the lessor against the tenant because of a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant has remedied the breach` IS FALSE,
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon the ground referred to in section 69` IS FALSE,
    `the consequences of the lessor continuing to be bound by the agreement would not be unduly burdensome to the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `within the period of 6 months before notice was given by the lessor the tenant complained to a public authority or took steps to secure or enforce the tenant's rights as a tenant` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has proved that the lessor was not wholly or partly motivated to give notice by that fact` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant is not eligible to reside in social housing premises or in the class of social housing premises to which the agreement relates under the criteria approved under section 71E` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has offered to enter into a new social housing tenancy agreement with the tenant in respect of alternative premises that are available for occupation by the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `any notice required to be given under section 71F or 71I before giving notice of termination was given in accordance with that section` IS FALSE,
    `any review required to be carried out under section 71F or 71I was carried out in accordance with that section` IS FALSE

`s.71 retaliatory notice` MEANS `section 71 application` WITH
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination to the other under this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given under section 70A` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the day specified` IS TRUE,
    `days after the day specified` IS 10,
    `the notice of termination was given immediately the rent breach occurred and the rent due is paid in full before the day specified` IS FALSE,
    `the notice complied with and was given in accordance with this Act` IS TRUE,
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon a particular ground prescribed by this Act` IS FALSE,
    `the notice was given by a lessor on a ground referred to in section 71C or 71H` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has established that ground` IS FALSE,
    `the notice was upon the ground of a breach by the tenant of a term of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the breach is in all the circumstances such as to justify termination of the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `giving the notice is retaliatory action taken by the lessor against the tenant because of a matter mentioned in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has remedied the breach` IS FALSE,
    `the notice was given by the lessor upon the ground referred to in section 69` IS FALSE,
    `the consequences of the lessor continuing to be bound by the agreement would not be unduly burdensome to the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `within the period of 6 months before notice was given by the lessor the tenant complained to a public authority or took steps to secure or enforce the tenant's rights as a tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has proved that the lessor was not wholly or partly motivated to give notice by that fact` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant is not eligible to reside in social housing premises or in the class of social housing premises to which the agreement relates under the criteria approved under section 71E` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor has offered to enter into a new social housing tenancy agreement with the tenant in respect of alternative premises that are available for occupation by the tenant` IS FALSE,
    `any notice required to be given under section 71F or 71I before giving notice of termination was given in accordance with that section` IS FALSE,
    `any review required to be carried out under section 71F or 71I was carried out in accordance with that section` IS FALSE

`s.72 120 day term holdover` MEANS `section 72 application` WITH
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination under section 70A` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the possession day` IS TRUE,
    `days after the possession day` IS 5,
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `the term of the tenancy under the agreement is less than 90 days` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor genuinely proposed at the time the lessor entered into the agreement to use the premises after the expiration of the term for purposes inconsistent with the tenant continuing to occupy the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant of the tenant's own initiative sought a tenancy of a term of less than 90 days` IS FALSE

`s.72 60 day term without exception` MEANS `section 72 application` WITH
    `the lessor or a tenant has given notice of termination under section 70A` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant failed to deliver up possession of the premises on the possession day` IS TRUE,
    `days after the possession day` IS 5,
    `the premises are the principal place of residence of the lessor` IS FALSE,
    `the term of the tenancy under the agreement is less than 90 days` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor genuinely proposed at the time the lessor entered into the agreement to use the premises after the expiration of the term for purposes inconsistent with the tenant continuing to occupy the premises` IS FALSE,
    `the tenant of the tenant's own initiative sought a tenancy of a term of less than 90 days` IS FALSE

`serious damage by tenant` MEANS `section 73 application` WITH
    `the applicant is the lessor` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, serious damage to the premises or, where relevant, a common area or chattels in the common area` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant has intentionally or recklessly caused or permitted, or is likely intentionally or recklessly to cause or permit, injury to the lessor, the property manager of the premises, or any person in occupation of or permitted on adjacent premises` IS FALSE

`tenant hardship` MEANS `section 74 application` WITH
    `the applicant is the lessor or the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor or tenant would in the circumstances of the case suffer undue hardship if required to terminate the agreement under any other provision of this Act` IS TRUE

`lessor quiet enjoyment breach justifying termination` MEANS `section 75 application` WITH
    `the applicant is the tenant` IS TRUE,
    `the lessor has breached the agreement` IS TRUE,
    `the breach is in the circumstances of the case such as to justify termination of the agreement` IS TRUE

#EVAL `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 71` `s.71 breach notice tenant still in possession`
#EVAL `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 71` `s.71 retaliatory notice`
#EVAL `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 72` `s.72 120 day term holdover`
#EVAL `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 72` `s.72 60 day term without exception`
#EVAL `the court may terminate the agreement under section 73` `serious damage by tenant`
#EVAL `the court may terminate the agreement under section 74` `tenant hardship`
#EVAL `the court may terminate the agreement under section 75` `lessor quiet enjoyment breach justifying termination`
#EVAL `an application under section 73, 74, 75A or 75 may be made whether or not notice of termination has been given`
#ASSERT `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 71` `s.71 breach notice tenant still in possession` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 71` `s.71 retaliatory notice` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 72` `s.72 120 day term holdover` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court shall make orders terminating the agreement and for possession under section 72` `s.72 60 day term without exception` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the court may terminate the agreement under section 73` `serious damage by tenant` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may terminate the agreement under section 74` `tenant hardship` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the court may terminate the agreement under section 75` `lessor quiet enjoyment breach justifying termination` EQUALS TRUE
